<title>UK: John Lewis weekly UK store sales up 20.3% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>John Lewis weekly UK store sales up 20.3% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership said on Friday its UK department store sales for the week to October 12 were up 20.3 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>For the 11 weeks to October 12, department store sales were up 16.7 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Total sales, including those from the Waitrose supermarket chain, rose 14.7 percent year-on-year. For the 11-week period, sales were up 13.0 percent.</p>
<p>-- Rosemary Bennett +44 171 542 7715</p>
